\section{Our Method}
Given a portrait image with cast shadows, our method aims to remove the facial shadows while faithfully preserving the facial details in the shadow regions. Figure~\ref{fig_inference} presents the overall inference pipeline of our method.

%The process begins with SE-Net extracting the clean face structure map of the input image, excluding shadow boundaries. Guided by this structure map, the shadow inpainting diffusion model (Inpaint Diff) generates an coarse shadow-removed output. The shadow mask is then refined by subtracting the shadow-removed output from the input and applying a reasonable threshold. Finally, the detail refinement diffusion model (Refine Diff) leverages the internal gradient information of the refined mask to restore high-quality details and achieve a shadow-free result.

