\max_{\bx\in\mathbb{R}^{n}_+}& \quad \sum_{i\in A} {\mu}_{i} \log(x_{i})   - \sum_{i\in A}\int_0^{x_i}t_i(y)\dif y \label{convex_optimization} \\
\text{s.t.} &\quad   x_i\le b_i,\quad\forall\>i\in A.\label{constraint:resource_i}
%\\    \text{over }& \bx = (x_{i})_{i\in A}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}_+,\nonumber
\end{align}
Since the objective function is strictly concave, the optimal solution is unique. Furthermore, the optimality conditions imply
%where $(x_i(\boldsymbol{\mu}))_{i\in A}$ is the unique optimal solution %and 
that the $w_i(\boldsymbol{\mu})$'s are the optimal Lagrange multipliers for the resource constraints  \eqref{constraint:resource_i}. A 
more detailed description of this fluid queueing model and a formal proof can be found in Appendix \ref{appendix:fluid_model}. Note that in this resource model, $x_i(\boldsymbol{\mu}) < x_i(\boldsymbol{\mu}')$ implies $x_i(\boldsymbol{\mu}) < b_i$ so $\tau_i(\boldsymbol{\mu}) = t_i(x_i(\bmu))\leq t_i(x_i(\bmu')) \leq \tau_i(\boldsymbol{\mu}')$. Thus, Assumption~\ref{assum_sojourntime} is satisfied.


