The existence of a stationary equilibrium is established in the following theorem.  


\begin{theorem}\label{thm:stationary_equilibrium}
There exists a stationary equilibrium for the game $\mathcal{G}$ with exponential discounting. Furthermore, $\boldsymbol{\mu}^\dagger$ is a stationary equilibrium of $\mathcal{G}$ if and only if 
\begin{equation}
\label{thm:stationary_equilibrium_eq}
    \frac{r_i}{e^{\beta \tau_i(\boldsymbol{\mu}^\dagger)}-1}\ge \frac{r_j}{e^{\beta \tau_j(\boldsymbol{\mu}^\dagger)}-1},\quad\forall\>i\in A^\dagger,\>j\in A,
\end{equation}
where $A^\dagger=\{i\in A\mid \mu^\dagger_i>0\}$.
