We consider a system where a common pool of agents choose between two independent actions  when they are free as depicted in Fig.~\ref{fig:twoaction}. We refer to this model as \emph{`two-action model'} in what follows.
 In the context of food delivery, this corresponds to a network with two hotspots, where couriers decide between two shopping mall areas. Once a courier becomes idle, they must decide which hotspot to relocate to in order to serve new orders.

