It follows that $\sigma^y\in\text{conv}(D(x))$ and hence $y\in\phi(x)$.

We have shown that $\phi$ is nonempty, convex and closed. It follows from Kakutani's fixed point theorem that $\phi$ has at least one fixed point and the first part of the theorem is proven. The second part of the theorem is obvious from the above proof.
