\[f_i=\frac{e^{\beta t_i}-1}{r_i}.\]
Then, $f_1<f_2<\cdots<f_n$, since we assume that $V_1> V_2>\cdots>V_n$.
Since the action execution times are constants, we only need to know the mass rates and waiting times at the equilibrium to obtain the corresponding mass distribution and strategies for the agents.  Under Assumption \ref{assum:constant_action_time}, the equilibrium results are given as follows. 

