Now we can choose $(r_1,r_2)\in\mathbb{R}_+^2$ such that
 \begin{equation}
     \frac{r_1}{e^{\beta \tau_1(\mu_1^\dagger)}-1}=\frac{r_2}{e^{\beta \tau_2(\mu_1^\dagger)}-1}.\label{condition:unstable_2_r}
 \end{equation}
Hence, for any $m>0$ and $\mu_1^\dagger\in(0,m)$, there exist $(t_1, t_2, r_1,r_2, \gamma_1,\gamma_2, $
