\subsection{Agent-environment specifications}\label{appendix:agent_environment_hyperparameters}
Our implementation leveraged the double deep-Q network (DDQN) algorithm with $n=5$ step trajectory roll-outs~\cite{sutton2018reinforcement}, employing a discount factor $\gamma=0.88$ and $\epsilon$-greedy exploration where $\epsilon$ decays geometrically from $1$ to $0.05$ (decay rate $0.99995$/step). The target network updated every $500$ steps, with unified hyperparameters across quantum systems: batch size $1000$, replay memory capacity $20,\!000$, ADAM optimizer~\cite{kingma2014adam} ($\eta=3\!\times\!10^{-4}$), and 5-layer neural networks ($1000$ neurons/layer). All TensorRL configurations used bond dimension $\chi=2$ unless explicitly varied, maintaining consistent entanglement patterns throughout the architecture search process. The number of steps (i.e. maximum number of gates allowed to add) per episode is provided in Tab.~\ref{tab:configs}, which shows that TensorRL-QAS requires less than half of the number of steps per episode for QAS tasks.
