\paragraph{Optimal Confidence Threshold Selection} %\hspace{0.2cm} 
Lastly, we find that the method is relatively insensitive to the choice of the temperature parameter $\tau$ across the range of values we considered. 
This robustness indicates that the effect of $\mathcal{L}_2^{\text{MI}}$--namely, propagating reliable information to more challenging instances--remains effective as long as $\tau$ is set within a reasonable range. 
In addition, our method does not require fine-tuning of $\tau$ to achieve strong performance, which improves usability in practical settings.

