\section{Introduction} %for journal use above \firstsection{..} instead
At the heart of topological data analysis lie so-called topological descriptors: summaries that identify important features of the data.
Topological descriptors are used in various application domains, such as medical imaging \cite{singh2023topological}, manufacturing~\cite{uray2024topological}, and environmental science~\cite{ver2023primer}.
They are generally classified into three types~\cite{yan2021scalar}: set-based descriptors such as persistence diagrams \cite{edelsbrunner2002topological}, complex-based descriptors including Morse-Smale complexes \cite{edelsbrunner2003hierarchical}, and graph-based descriptors such as Reeb graphs \cite{biasotti2008reeb, reeb1946points}.

