%where $(2^{At}, r_i(s), id)$ is a Kripke model (notice that the valuation function is the identity function $id$, as the truth assignment is expressed directly by the state), $v(s) \in 2^{At}$ is the state under analysis, and the interpretation of $\models$ is the standard one for the Kripke semantics of the knowledge operator.
